    "turn_text": "next year. You guys don't know Jersey has off years or like an off year election from the presidential cycle for their governors races. So yeah. Something to look forward to in 2025, be to dubs. Like there are some seriously wild elections coming after this election. So crazy. But without getting too distracted, we chatted with the Congresswoman about Repro and specifically Repro in the military and just the lay of blame of that. We realized we hadn't quite covered that. So it's a little sort of that without further ado, here is Congresswoman Cheryl. All right. Welcome to Girl in the Gove. I genuinely almost just said call her daddy. First of all, which is not our podcast because of calm layers going on call her daddy. But more importantly, we have Congressman Cheryl from New Jersey, which is my original home state. So I'm very excited about this on Girl in the Gove today. And we are going to really dive into reproductive rights. Now, This has been one of those conversations that we've been chatting about for truly the last number of years and beyond, but especially in the post-row era. And one of the areas that we haven't focused on quite enough is how this impacts our service members. So we know that you definitely have an eye on this area. Can you tell us what the post-row era situation has been like for our service members?",
