    "turn_idx": 125,
    "turn_text": "That is so well said. You know, I have had women who fought for Roe initially about 50 years ago. And they would say, they would speak about abortion as a freedom, as basic bodily autonomy. And I don't know. I just had trouble seeing it that way, I guess. I just had abortion was abortion. I was just, you know, health care. But they would speak about it far more broadly as far as your rights and what you have a right to. And do you have a right to have somebody else control you in that way? And I will tell you now, after the fall of Roe, I understand it so clearly. When you see legislators trying to control women, trying to say that if you are on a county road, and they can catch you trying to seek an abortion that you can be arrested for that. How are they going to know? What is that control that they are going to exert over you? Trying to say that women can't travel for abortion. What does that look like in practice? Are you going to get a medical exam every time you try to fly when you're a woman of a certain age? What if you have a miscarriage when you're out of town and you have to come back and report to the police and get a medical doctor to say, oh, no, this was a miscarriage, not an abortion. I mean, that is what we're fee-gilling as we talk about our freedom, but just beyond those cases of some lawmakers that are trying to implement that in some of our states. But to just see that here I have people in my state of New Jersey, which has very good reproductive protections for women, that women are being asked to go take a business trip as they're pregnant to a place like Texas or to a place like Florida or Idaho and you know they're saying to their employer I'm pregnant I can't go and there are cases now in court where this is being litigated like can you make a person go to another state in this country, so you're seeing your rights in certain states in this country, circumscribed as a woman, which is really scary when you feel like, as I was saying to someone, it feels like your citizenship is now only a partial citizenship. You can only enjoy your full citizenship in a state like New Jersey, but if you're a woman, especially pregnant women. You can't have full freedoms in other states. You can't make your own decisions.",
