    "turn_text": "overturned Roe. And so we know that this is going to be something that should Trump ever be in the White House. Again, women will be even more endangered. So we've got to get Kamala Harris across the finish line. Beyond that, we also have to flip the House of Representatives. As a member of the House of Representatives, I have to tell you that the current majority is ineffective, not competent, almost unable to govern. It's why we still don't have any of our appropriations bills passed. We sort of gave up. I think I've seen some statistics that we have taken more votes and gotten less done than any Congress in the history of the country. It's like a sense of constant churn, just trying to throw red meat to the far right maga people. in the hopes we could eat some things across the finish line, like just what we call a continuing resolution, which is how we just kind of keep kind of kick the can down the road on our appropriations bills, just to keep the government open to try to get past the selection. We saw that under Trump's guidance, they undermined much of what we tried to do with a border compromise. We've seen the difficulty we had in passing a supplemental. So Ukraine was in a far worse position than when we if we had just passed it at the beginning when we tried to do that. So again, and again, and again, we've seen this inability to govern. So flipping the house of representatives is critically important as well. And that's where a lot of the focus is, certainly my focus is and around New Jersey, what we're focused on right now.",
