    "turn_text": "Yeah. I always do. And this is like by no means accurate. So like nobody come and like say, try and be a stem girl. Like I am not, but whenever I'm out in the suburbs and I'm driving around and I'm seeing yard signs, that's usually like my, my go to counting method. And you see, especially if you're going over the same areas or you're like where your parents are from or whatever, you see that shift in what the yard signs are doing, election cycle over election cycle. Like this particular one, I am seeing dem signs and places I've never seen them. And that in and of itself, I think really speaks volumes, like places where you're like, oh, that is so red. And Jersey has some red areas which no one talks about. Nobody talks about. Like my parents literally used to live in Mendum and there was like Trump corner where they were living. So it is honestly sort of a misnomer and I am curious just like bring it back to Jersey for a second. People that don't know the realm of Jersey, North, Central, South, all of the things. What would you describe the political environments or of landscape of the state?",
