  {
    "episode_id": 95653,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95653.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 157,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, so I think. I think we all have to work incredibly hard to ensure people know how to vote, know that their vote counts. I think we are kind of gearing up for more and more misinformation coming out from Niagara Republicans. We're trying to undermine our system right now. We saw it. In the last election, in fact, our own speaker of the House was the architect of an amicus brief full of misinformation about voting. So we're going to see some of this pushed out and I think making sure that all voters here in New Jersey know the system feel confident in the system and know how their vote is going to be registered and going to count is very important. When I was on, I kicked off a bus as they were headed into Pennsylvania. So I got on the bus and one woman said to me, you know what, Mikey? This is doing something. So as we all heard from Kamala Harris do something, that's what we've got to continue to do. So if you can get on a bus and get into one of the swing states, great. If you can phone bank, if you can write some postcards. If you can just have conversations with your neighbors about what it is, you think, The Democratic ticket represents and why it's so important. Go do something. Go have those conversations. Go knock on those doors. And I think we're going to really see some great results. Let's face it, these have been some really tough years with COVID, with everything going on in the world. A lot of people feel a little overwhelmed. So if you're finding that in your neighbors and friends, Focus on some of the local elections. Focus on what's going on in your town and the great representatives that you're trying to elect in your town or what they've been delivering in your town, because that's also important, I think, to build that sense of not being overwhelmed and then people can vote up ticket. So we're doing all those things here. And like I said, I'm feeling really good on the ground here in Jersey.",
